      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 101,
      "outputTokens": 807,
      "costUsd": 0.0073135000000000006,
      "pronunciationText": "First, make the equation simpler. Twelve plus two sine of the bracket equals thirteen, so take twelve from both sides: two sine of the bracket equals one. Divide by two, and sine of the bracket equals a half. Sliding both graphs down, then squashing both, moves the curve and the line together, so the crossings stay at exactly the same x values. Now the question is: where does sine of x minus pi over six equal a half, for x from zero to two pi?"
