      "costUsd": 0.009298500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Call the inside u, so u equals x minus pi over six. When x runs from zero to two pi, u runs from minus pi over six to eleven pi over six. That's the window we search on the plain sine curve. Sine u is a half at pi over six, and, by symmetry about the peak, at five pi over six. The next ones, thirteen pi over six and minus seven pi over six, are outside the window. Now undo the substitution: x is u plus pi over six. So x is pi over three, or pi: a sixth of the way through the year, and halfway. That's the same slide right by pi over six that we saw for the graph."
    },
