      "inputTokens": 108,
      "outputTokens": 788,
      "costUsd": 0.0071460000000000004,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's why counting works. In one cycle, the curve rises through every height between its lowest and highest values once, and falls through it once. So a line strictly between them crosses twice per cycle, unless an end of the domain lands on it, which we check next. Raise the line to fourteen hours, the longest day, and it only touches, once per cycle. Raise it to fourteen and a half, and no day has that much daylight at all. So count the cycles, and check where the line sits."
    },
