      "inputTokens": 129,
      "outputTokens": 998,
      "costUsd": 0.0090465,
      "pronunciationText": "But watch the ends of the domain. Solve two cos of x minus pi over four equals root two, from zero to two pi, with both ends included. Cos of the bracket is root two over two. The window for u runs from minus pi over four to seven pi over four. Cos u is root two over two at pi over four, but also at minus pi over four and seven pi over four, the two ends of the window. So x is zero, pi over two, and two pi. That's three solutions in one cycle, because both ends of the domain are included, and both land on the line."
