      "outputTokens": 1152,
      "costUsd": 0.0104375,
      "pronunciationText": "Graphs also answer questions that algebra finds awkward. For which values of k does two sine of x minus pi over six equal k exactly twice, for x from zero to two pi? Slide a level line up and down. The curve starts and ends at minus one: the same date, a year apart. It rises to two, and falls to minus two. Between minus one and two, the line crosses twice. Between minus two and minus one, it crosses twice too. But at exactly minus one, it also hits both ends, giving three, and at two or minus two, it only touches. So k is between minus two and minus one, or between minus one and two."
    },
