      "pronunciationText": "Tan works the same way, with one crossing on each complete branch. Solve tan two x equals one, for x from zero to pi. Let u equal two x, so u runs from zero to two pi. Tan repeats every pi, so tan u is one at pi over four, and again at five pi over four. Halve them: x is pi over eight, or five pi over eight. The asymptotes, at pi over four and three pi over four, are never solutions, because tan isn't defined there."
