      "costUsd": 0.0077044999999999995,
      "pronunciationText": "You can check any of these on a graphing app. Plot both sides, and read the crossings. For the first example, the app shows about one point zero four seven and three point one four two, which match pi over three and pi. The graph answers inequalities too. The curve is above the line between those crossings, so two sine of x minus pi over six is at least one for x from pi over three to pi. The app gives decimals, the algebra gives exact values, and the graph tells you how many to expect."
